// REJECTS: Unexpected token '('. Valid alternatives: ['extends', 'projects', '[', '<']
//
// A Class body is BRACES. Every store-side construct in the language -- Database, Mapping,
// View, Table -- is parens, and one section header away from here `Mapping x ( ... )` is
// correct. This is the single most likely delimiter to be got wrong by muscle memory, in
// either direction (mapping-braces-not-parens.pure pins the mirror).
//
// The alternatives list is the useful part to keep: after a class's qualified name the
// grammar accepts exactly extends, projects, '[' (constraints) or '<' (type parameters).
// Not '('. A rewrite that treats brackets interchangeably has no reason to ever notice.
###Pure
Class fixture::neg::ParenBody
(
   code: String[1];
)
